!Sample_hyb_protocol	"GeneChip microarrays are loaded with the fragmented target sample/hybridization buffer mix using standard manual techniques. Arrays are hybridized for 18 hours at 45oC with vigorous mixing. Unbound sample is removed and staining is accomplished through the binding of streptavidin conjugated phycoerythrin to the hybridized target. Excess label is removed. Washing and staining steps are performed by the Affymetrix FS450 fluidics station using standard protocols."	"GeneChip microarrays are loaded with the fragmented target sample/hybridization buffer mix using standard manual techniques. Arrays are hybridized for 18 hours at 45oC with vigorous mixing. Unbound sample is removed and staining is accomplished through the binding of streptavidin conjugated phycoerythrin to the hybridized target. Excess label is removed. Washing and staining steps are performed by the Affymetrix FS450 fluidics station using standard protocols."	"GeneChip microarrays are loaded with the fragmented target sample/hybridization buffer mix using standard manual techniques. Arrays are hybridized for 18 hours at 45oC with vigorous mixing. Unbound sample is removed and staining is accomplished through the binding of streptavidin conjugated phycoerythrin to the hybridized target. Excess label is removed. Washing and staining steps are performed by the Affymetrix FS450 fluidics station using standard protocols."	"GeneChip microarrays are loaded with the fragmented target sample/hybridization buffer mix using standard manual techniques. Arrays are hybridized for 18 hours at 45oC with vigorous mixing. Unbound sample is removed and staining is accomplished through the binding of streptavidin conjugated phycoerythrin to the hybridized target. Excess label is removed. Washing and staining steps are performed by the Affymetrix FS450 fluidics station using standard protocols."	"GeneChip microarrays are loaded with the fragmented target sample/hybridization buffer mix using standard manu